WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.333
Cybersecurity training. Module 3. Phishing and social engineering.

2
00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:10.000
Attackers target people, not only computers.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.700
Urgency, fear and authority are the usual tricks.

4
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.933
Phishing: an email that pretends to be someone you trust.

5
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.733
Spear phishing: the same, but written for you.

6
00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.933
Smishing: the same by text message.

7
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.733
When a request asks for money, access or patient information, stop.

8
00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:35.233
A voice or a face is not proof of who is asking,

9
00:00:35.233 --> 00:00:39.900
because criminals use software to make convincing fake audio and video.

10
00:00:40.267 --> 00:00:43.400
Check it another way: call back on a number you already

11
00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:46.500
know, or ask in a chat channel the client already uses.

12
00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:52.167
Never use the number or link that came with the request, and tell your lead.

13
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:59.167
If you clicked or answered, report it immediately. Speed limits the damage.

14
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:01.167
Pause.

15
00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:02.400
Verify.

16
00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:03.867
Report fast.

17
00:01:04.267 --> 00:01:06.000
Now read the module.
